            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_34c6ba61">
               <extent xml:id="extent_8ead9795">72 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_c95f43fd">25.5 x 35</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_b834241c">Bound in purple cardboard with handwritten label: "Orgelets Priis 1826 / Til Julefesten 1827 / Til Paaskefesten 1828. Partitur." Written in brown ink. Paper: 12 staves. All three works consecutively paginated 1-70. This work is on pp. 45-70 followed by 2 blank, unnumbered pages. On p. 45 in pencil: "Til Paaskefesten". On p. 49 after the last bar of No. 1: "1827". Page 50 blank. On p. 51 an alternative ending to No. 1. Inserted between pp. 64 and 67 a folio in foreign hand which does not belong to this work, but has been paginated 65-66. On p. 70 end-dated "d: 7/3 28". On the last, unpaginated page in Hartmann's hand: "Underlige, svage Hjerte / Mellem Gud og Verden deelt / har Du i Fryd og Smerte / Ingen Dig hengivet heelt. / Denne jammerlige Svæven / Mellem Jord og Himlens Borg, / Den er Aarsag til Din Bæven, den er Kilden til Din Sorg."</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
